PART 2 -- FIX 1: SELECT ... FOR UPDATE on the daily_capacity row
========================================================================
[  0.12s] reset: Lekki on the demo day is now 38/40 units used
[  0.13s] A took the row lock; A reads 38/40
[  0.13s] B asks for the same row lock ... (it will have to wait)
[  1.63s] A inserts its 2-tier order and COMMITs (this releases the lock)
[  1.63s] B got the lock after waiting 1.50s; B now reads 40/40
[  1.63s] B decides: day fully booked -> ROLLBACK (no overbooking)
[  1.64s] RESULT: 40/40 units used  <-- never overbooked

========================================================================
PART 3 -- FIX 2: SERIALIZABLE isolation + retry on SQLSTATE 40001
========================================================================
[  1.67s] reset: Lekki on the demo day is now 38/40 units used
[  1.68s] A reads 38/40, B reads 38/40 (both SERIALIZABLE)
[  1.68s] A inserted a 2-tier order
[  1.69s] B inserted a 2-tier order
[  1.69s] A COMMIT -> succeeded
[  1.69s] B COMMIT -> FAILED  SQLSTATE 40001: could not serialize access due to read/write dependencies among transactions
[  1.69s] B retries in a new SERIALIZABLE transaction
[  1.69s] B re-reads 40/40 -> day fully booked, order refused
[  1.69s] RESULT: 40/40 units used  <-- never overbooked

